== Slots ==

Every item has a '''slot type''' (internal enum <code>Slot_Type</code> in the <code>Item_Info</code> assembly) that determines where it can go. Human Host uses a hand-based equipment model where weapons and tools go into a left- or right-hand slot rather than a generic hotbar.

{| class="wikitable"
! Slot !! Purpose
|-
| '''Nothing''' || Ignored / no-slot marker (used for unequipped or purely storage items)
|-
| '''Hand_R''' || Right hand (primary weapon or tool)
|-
| '''Hand_L''' || Left hand (off-hand weapon, shield, torch)
|-
| '''Equip''' || Wearable equipment (armor, headlamp, backpack)
|-
| '''Ammo''' || Ammunition routed to the current weapon
|-
| '''GunAttach''' || Firearm attachments (scopes, silencers, magazines)
|-
| '''Merchant''' || Reserved for merchant NPC inventory (system not yet surfaced in the current build)
|}

== Tags ==

Items carry '''tags''' (an <code>Icon_Info._Tags</code> array). Tags drive:

* '''Recipe matching''': a "wood" recipe accepts any tagged wood item
* '''Cross-references''': search by tag on this wiki (planned)

Common tags: <code>wood</code>, <code>stone</code>, <code>metal</code>, <code>ore</code>, <code>ingot</code>, <code>ammo</code>, <code>fuel</code>.

== Weight ==

Items weigh: carry too much and you slow down and lose stamina faster. Weight is stored per-item; heavier items (metal ingots, ammunition) discourage over-hoarding without a vehicle or base storage.

== Stacking ==

Most items stack. Stack sizes vary. Some items (weapons with durability, unique items) do not stack.

